# Player Modifiers configuration
#
# This file defines global multiplicative modifiers applied to all players' attributes
# after base stats, items, passives, buffs, and transformations are calculated.
#
# Usage:
# - Copy to PlayerModifiers.cfg and edit values. Any missing key defaults to 1.0 (no change).
# - To enable this system, set `Enabled=1` (default is 0/disabled).
# - Scopes supported (put modifiers after the colon):
#     all modifiers: hp=1.10 physAtk=1.05 engDef=0.95          # global
#     char 12345 modifiers: physAtk=1.20 engDef=0.90           # by CharacterID
#     name Goku modifiers: runSpd=1.15 physCrit=1.10           # by Character Name (case-insensitive)
#
# Keys:
#   hp, physAtk, engAtk, physDef, engDef,
#   atkSpd, runSpd, physCrit, engCrit, physCritDmg, engCritDmg,
#   attackRate, dodgeRate, blockRate, blockDmg, guardRate
#
# Notes:
# - Attack speed is a rate where lower is faster. A value < 1.0 increases attack speed.
# - These modifiers are applied on every stat recalculation and are not persisted.

# Master switch (0 = disabled, 1 = enabled)
Enabled=0

# Example: modest global boost
all modifiers: hp=1.05 physAtk=1.03 engAtk=1.03 physDef=1.02 engDef=1.02 runSpd=1.02

# Example: per-player overrides
# Character ID 1001 gets strong attack buff
char 1001 modifiers: physAtk=1.25 engAtk=1.20 physCrit=1.15 physCritDmg=1.10
# Character named "Goku" gets faster movement and guard
name Goku modifiers: runSpd=1.20 guardRate=1.10
